index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..53d97ce193433c37091805df189c9c02868020ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/patch-radv-series/lead-mesh-45-radv-mesh-points-as-compute.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,389 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: EglantinePS5
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: EDEN_UP_RADV_MESH_POINTS=1 runs mesh shaders of points and lines as compute
+
+Driver patch, after lead-mesh-44 in tools/patch-radv-series. Off unless the switch is set.
+
+Port of zortos293/Lichii bc45e10 (PR #863, "draw points and lines through the mesh compute
+fallback", by nemiward). Upstream's change is in its core's own compute fallback; ours runs mesh
+shaders as compute in the driver (lead-mesh-05/09), which took triangles only and dropped the rest.
+Ocarina draws its plant shadow map (1600x1600) with a mesh program of points, two draws a frame in
+the field, so grass and bushes cast no shadow.
+
+- radv_mesh_compute_wanted takes points and lines with the switch on, and a point size output for
+  points. =2 also takes a triangle program that writes a point size (left out of the slots).
+- The slots keep one dword of indices per primitive as before; the copy vertex shader reads k = 1
+  (points) or 2 (lines) of them per primitive instead of 3, copies a point's size, and the copy
+  draw (compile-time state and the draw's topology) is a point or line list.
+- An unused slot of a point or a line goes behind the eye (w = -1, size 0), outside every clip
+  plane. Upstream found a repeated index draws such points, and moving them just outside the view
+  was not enough on RADV (the guard band); it used a clip distance, this uses w < 0.
+- The cache keeps the primitive in the top byte of the vertex count: 0 for triangles, so every
+  saved entry reads as before. With the switch on these pipelines' hash takes
+  RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_POINTS_REVISION and the switch's value (a point program compiled before was
+  refused); unset, no hash changes.
+- Lines: "radv/ps5: EDEN_UP_RADV_MESH_POINTS: mesh shader of points runs as compute (...)" per
+  pipeline compiled (32 at most), and "radv/ps5: EDEN_UP_RADV_MESH_POINTS draws=N (points P, lines L)"
+  at 1, 2, 4, 8 ... draws.
+
+The core refuses point and line programs unless EDEN_NX2_MESH_POINTS=1 (patch 0173), so both are
+needed. Triangle pipelines compile to the same code as before, switch on or off.
+
+Co-Authored-By: nemiward (zortos293/Lichii PR #863)
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
+---
+diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
+index d8af00b..ce73f4a 100644
+--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
++++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
+@@ -15908,7 +15908,13 @@ radv_mesh_compute_draw(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer, const struct radv_dra
+    const uint64_t block_va = radv_buffer_get_va(cmd_buffer->upload.upload_bo) + block_offset;
+ 
+    const uint32_t saved_topology = d->vk.ia.primitive_topology;
+-   d->vk.ia.primitive_topology = V_008958_DI_PT_TRILIST;
++   /* EDEN_UP_RADV_MESH_POINTS: a pipeline of points or lines draws a point or line list. */
++   const uint32_t prim_vertices = pipeline->mesh_compute_prim_vertices;
++   d->vk.ia.primitive_topology = prim_vertices == 1   ? V_008958_DI_PT_POINTLIST
++                                 : prim_vertices == 2 ? V_008958_DI_PT_LINELIST
++                                                      : V_008958_DI_PT_TRILIST;
++   if (prim_vertices == 1 || prim_vertices == 2)
++      radv_mesh_compute_note_points_draw(prim_vertices);
+    state->dirty_dynamic |= RADV_DYNAMIC_PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY;
+    state->dirty |= RADV_CMD_DIRTY_VGT_PRIM_STATE;
+ 
